<title>USA: CIT Group issues $100 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>CIT Group issues $100 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from CIT Group Holdings Inc was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p>CIT Group Holdings, a consumer finance concern, is 80 percent owned by Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd and 20 percent owned by Chase Manhattan Corp.</p>
<p>BORROWER CIT GROUP HOLDINGS INC</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON 6.70 PCT   MATURITY 5/02/2000</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.895  FIRST PAY DATE 11/02/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD 6.739 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 26 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
